CONVENTION NOTE (binding decision — no scope narrowing, no predecessor bypass)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Analytics/
PeriodComparePage.swift` + a `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog. Those are
generator idealizations: the REAL, current convention used by every completed P7
analytics sibling on this branch (FleetComparePage, StatisticsPage, TrueCostPage)
is:
  - pages under `apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/` (multi-file split)
  - the CENTRAL string catalog `apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings`
  - an `AppRoute` case + a `*RouteRegistration` enum wired in `TeslaSyncApp`
  - tests under `apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/<Domain>/`
I followed the `FleetComparePage` sibling template EXACTLY (it is the closest
analog — a compare page with selectors + metric cards + bar chart + comparison
table + insights + the disambiguation banner). This keeps the surface buildable
within the existing `project.yml` source globs and consistent with shipped code.
The `apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/` mega-dump (e.g. AlertStudioPage) is the
older parallel-surface layout; the Sources/Features layout supersedes it for P7.

