--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
IMPLEMENTATION NOTES (fidelity)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Data binding: web `useVehicles` (GET /vehicles) + `request('/analytics/period-stats
  ?vehicle_id=&days=')` are modeled by the `PeriodCompareDataSource` seam (ADR-004);
  the @Observable `PeriodComparePageModel` owns vehicle list + active vehicle + A/B
  window selection + both periods' stats + the banner; production binds the KMP core,
  previews/tests inject doubles. No networking in the view.
- SI cutover (ADR-005): the model stores SI canonical (meters, watt-hours, Wh/km);
  `PeriodCompareFormat` converts at the render boundary via the shared `Units` facade
  + `@Environment(\.tsUnits)`. Distance→km/mi, energy→Wh/kWh, efficiency→Wh/km|Wh/mi.
- Adaptive (ADR-002/006): selectors reflow HStack (regular) ↔ VStack (compact);
  metric grid is an adaptive LazyVGrid; table is a SwiftUI Grid.
- HIG/a11y (ADR-015): tokens-only colors/typography (no hardcoded), VoiceOver labels
  + header traits on panels/chart/table, Dynamic Type via teslaSyncTheme(), light/dark
  + high-contrast via the dynamic `Color.TS` tokens, ≥44pt native controls.
- i18n (ADR-014): every visible literal is a LocalizedStringKey resolving from
  Localizable.xcstrings under the web key names; the 3 insight templates preserve the
  web i18next `{{pct}}`/`{{dir}}` tokens (substituted with localized direction words).
- Navigation: `.periodCompare` route (pathSegment "period-compare") + AppRouteParser
  alias "/period-compare" → deep-linkable; registered in TeslaSyncApp via
  PeriodCompareRouteRegistration; banner dismissal persisted (UserDefaults key
  "phase40.compareBanner.dismissed.period", web localStorage parity).
- No live SSE: neither data source is live (vehicles + period roll-ups), so no SSE
  subscription / staleness indicator is required (ADR-013 N/A for this surface).

